Day 24 – Advanced Git 🚀

Today I learned some important Git concepts that are widely used in real projects.

Topics Covered

- Git Merge
- Fast-Forward Merge
- Merge Commit
- Merge Conflict
- Git Rebase
- Squash Merge
- Git Stash
- Git Cherry-Pick

What I Practiced

✅ Created multiple branches

✅ Merged branches using both Fast-Forward and Merge Commit

✅ Created and resolved a Merge Conflict

✅ Used Rebase to keep commit history clean

✅ Learned the difference between Merge and Rebase

✅ Practiced Squash Merge

✅ Saved unfinished work using Git Stash and restored it later

✅ Applied a specific commit using Git Cherry-Pick

Key Learnings

- Merge combines branches.
- Rebase creates a cleaner commit history.
- Squash Merge combines multiple commits into one.
- Stash temporarily saves unfinished work.
- Cherry-Pick copies a specific commit to another branch.

Every day I am improving my Git and DevOps skills through hands-on practice. 💻

